1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,368
Overnight rain turned the stream to mud.

2
00:00:03,901 --> 00:00:05,881
But the rain falling from the sky is clean.

3
00:00:07,174 --> 00:00:08,923
From my pack, I take out one tarp.

4
00:00:09,899 --> 00:00:12,098
I tie its four corners high on the trees,

5
00:00:13,593 --> 00:00:15,567
and let the middle sag low, like a funnel.

6
00:00:17,324 --> 00:00:18,452
Beneath it, I dig a pit.

7
00:00:19,197 --> 00:00:20,399
Bori happily digs too.

8
00:00:21,296 --> 00:00:24,491
I pack clay onto the floor and walls, and pound it firm.

9
00:00:24,945 --> 00:00:26,919
The clay keeps the water from leaking out.

10
00:00:27,624 --> 00:00:30,006
When the rain returns, water gathers on the tarp.

11
00:00:31,572 --> 00:00:33,497
It runs down in a stream into the pit.

12
00:00:34,473 --> 00:00:36,788
I cover it with bark, so no leaves fall in.

13
00:00:38,649 --> 00:00:41,384
Still, before drinking, I boil it once in the pot.

14
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:44,542
Now there's water without walking to the stream.

15
00:00:44,884 --> 00:00:46,074
One tarp became a well.

